    "result": "I implemented `parse_line` in `solution.py` following `spec.md`, and wrote 51 pytest tests in `tests/test_solution.py`; `python -m pytest -q tests` passes all of them. The function checks that `line` and `sep` are strings (`TypeError`), then that `sep` is exactly one character and not `\"`, CR or LF (`ValueError`). It then scans left to right: a field starting with `\"` runs to the next undoubled quote, with `\"\"` becoming one quote and separators and CR/LF kept as ordinary characters. Anything other than `sep` directly after a closing quote is an error. Unquoted fields run to the next separator, and a `\"`, `\\r` or `\\n` inside one raises `ValueError`. Whitespace is never trimmed, and `k` separators outside quotes give `k + 1` fields. The tests cover the spec's examples, custom separators, the error cases, and the edge cases (empty line, trailing and leading separators, unclosed quotes, stray quotes, CR/LF placement). I only wrote `solution.py` and files under `tests/`, and installed nothing.",
